00:00:01.829 --> 00:00:03.590 align:start position:0%
justin trudeau wanted to meet face to  face today with as many commonwealth  leaders as he could and he literally  went from a to z starting with the prime  minister of antigua and barbuda and  finishing with the president of zambia  my dear brother justin certainly a  pleasure the top priority for the 30 or  so island states here getting big  countries like canada to help with  climate change it is the most  significant threat facing the caribbean  region trudeau is sympathetic always a  pleasure to sit down with a friend from  the caribbean but trudeau's bigger  mission here is to convince leaders of  the 10 commonwealth states that  abstained when the u.n voted to condemn  russia's invasion of ukraine to change  their minds canada believes that adding  the censure of the commonwealth  representing 54 countries and more than  2 billion people will help ukraine one  argument canada is making connect the  dots between russia's illegal invasion  and food shortages many african and  caribbean nations are facing as a result  indeed all leaders here spent about half  the day discussing food security and  food price inflation but it will be  difficult for trudeau to find a  commonwealth consensus on russia and  ukraine because so many key leaders  skipped this summit india and south  africa for example abstained at the u.n  on the russia vote and neither country's  leader is at this summit but officials  tell us they're worried that the word  ukraine may not even be in the final  statement or communique that will be  issued tomorrow when the summit wraps up  farah  david aiken and rwanda thank you david
 

